== basic printing

Gnucap has built-in print commands, but Verilog offers some more flexibility,
and a more standard way to tailor data files.

$ gnucap-mg-vams --cc printer0.vams | g++ -xc++ `gnucap-conf --cppflags` -fPIC -shared - -o printer0.so
$ gnucap printer0.gc
[..]

